AssignReviewer.requestParamsDescription:
### JsonStr parameter details

| Property       | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                   |
| :------------- | :----- | :------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| assignmentList | List   | No       | List of files to assign. Files are assigned one by one. This field and searchParam cannot both be empty. If both are provided, assignmentList takes precedence. For details, see **assignmentList structure** |
| searchParam    | Object | No       | Filter conditions. These match the request parameters of [GetResult](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/142334.html). Use them to select files for batch assignment.                                     |
| assignments    | List   | No       | Reviewer information. Used during batch assignment to specify reviewers. For details, see **Assignments structure**                                                                                           |

#### assignmentList structure

| Property | Type   | Required | Description                                        |
| :------- | :----- | :------- | :------------------------------------------------- |
| taskId   | String | Yes      | Task ID of the file                                |
| fileId   | String | Yes      | File ID                                            |
| reviewer | String | No       | Reviewer ID. Used only for single-file assignment. |

#### Assignments structure

| Property | Type   | Required | Description                                                        |
| :------- | :----- | :------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| reviewer | String | Yes      | Reviewer ID                                                        |
| count    | String | No       | Number of files to assign. If empty, files are distributed evenly. |

### Request examples

#### 1. Distribute multiple files evenly among multiple reviewers

```
{
        "assignmentList":[
            {
                "taskId":"1C21CF1E-2917-4236-A046-20E37B293B69",
                "fileId":"7981b466fd6a4c70a7065da159739a5b"
            },
            {
                "taskId":"0111DDBC-5F10-47E0-B7D4-7175F47D626F",
                "fileId":"1814eeae3cff41e989e31ab547f07561"
            }
        ],
        "assignments":[
            {
                "reviewer":"255746168704895558"
            },
            {
                "reviewer":"268370362815185444"
            }
        ]
}
```

#### 2. Assign a specific number of files to each reviewer

Assign multiple files to multiple reviewers, specifying how many files each reviewer receives.

```
{
        "assignmentList":[
            {
                "taskId":"C97132A8-F0C5-4FA3-83C3-8C145CECB8C1",
